<title>USA: AST Research president/CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>AST Research president/CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>AST Research Inc, which is being acquired by Samsung Electronics Co Ltd, said Monday it had named a Samsung executive to replace AST President and Chief Executive Young Soo (Y.S.) Kim, who resigned.</p>
<p>Soon-Taek Kim, formerly chief executive officer of Samsung Heavy Industries Co Ltd, will lead AST, company said.</p>
<p>Young Soo Kim, who is resigning the positions for personal reasons, will remain as an AST board member, the company said.</p>
<p>Last week AST said it would cut its workforce by 25 percent and take $12 million in charges after posting lower-than-expected first quarter earnings. It said earnings were hurt by lower demand and customer uncertainty surrounding the Samsung deal.</p>
</text>
